# Branch and PR workflow

`develop` and `main` are **protected**. Do not commit on them or push to them.

## Required flow

1. Start from up-to-date `develop`: `git fetch origin && git checkout develop && git pull --ff-only origin develop`
2. Create a feature branch: `git checkout -b cursor/<short-topic>` (or `feat/…`)
3. Commit only on that branch
4. Push the branch and open a PR into `develop` with `gh pr create`
5. Never `git push origin develop` / `main`

If work was accidentally committed on `develop`, move it to a branch (`git branch <name>` then `git reset --hard origin/develop`) before opening the PR.
